.SH "SIGNALS"
.PP
.TS
allbox;
lbw(0.9i) lbx
lw(0.9i) lx.
T{
Signal
T}	T{
Effect
T}
T{
\fBSIGHUP\fR
T}	T{
Reload the configuration. A new generation is built and validated first;\: on error the running one stays active and the failure is counted. Listeners are added,\: removed and rebuilt as the file changed;\: see the reload semantics in \fBxproxy.\:yaml\fR(5).
T}
T{
\fBSIGUSR1\fR
T}	T{
Reopen the log files (used by logrotate).
T}
T{
\fBSIGTERM\fR,\: \fBSIGINT\fR
T}	T{
Stop: listeners close,\: in\-flight requests get \fBserver.\:shutdown_\:timeout\fR to finish,\: then the process exits.
T}
.TE
.PP
Under systemd use \fBsystemctl reload xproxy\fR and \fBsystemctl restart xproxy\fR; the unit maps them to these signals and socket activation keeps the listening sockets across a restart.
